    "title": "Executable or script run from a world-writable temp dir",
    "desc": "A process executed out of a world-writable scratch dir - either its own image lives under /tmp, /dev/shm, /var/tmp or /run/user (a dropped payload run directly, or through its shebang), or an interpreter (bash, sh, python, perl ...) was handed a script PATH under one of those dirs. Legitimate programs are installed under /usr, /bin or the nix store and run from there; staging a payload in a scratch dir and executing it is a classic post-download step. The executable LOCATION is the signal - this deliberately does NOT fire on an interpreter that merely mentions a temp path inside inline `-c` code (only a temp script-file argument counts).",
